# Sezaba CI styling

This monorepo uses a **fixed 6-color palette**. All UI must use these tokens — never introduce arbitrary hex values or default Tailwind palette colors (`blue-500`, `zinc-200`, `slate-900`, etc.).

## Palette

| Token | Hex | Role |
|-------|-----|------|
| `brand-black` | `#000000` | Text, default buttons (light mode) |
| `brand-white` | `#FFFFFF` | Primary light background |
| `brand-beige` | `#F3F3EB` | Secondary light background, muted surfaces |
| `brand-pink` | `#FEC6E9` | Light background accent, chart/data accent |
| `brand-red` | `#D20001` | **Default** accent (CTAs, highlights, charts, destructive) |
| `brand-blue` | `#0212EE` | Secondary accent (charts, data viz) |

## Semantic tokens (prefer these)

Use shadcn semantic classes so components stay theme-aware:

- **Page**: `bg-background text-foreground`
- **Default button**: `bg-primary text-primary-foreground` (black on light, white on dark)
- **Secondary surfaces**: `bg-secondary`, `bg-muted`
- **Highlight panels**: `bg-accent text-accent-foreground` (pink)
- **Errors / destructive**: `bg-destructive`, `text-destructive`, `border-destructive`
- **Charts**: `chart-1` (red) → `chart-5` (beige) — see `STYLEGUIDE.md`

Direct brand utilities when semantics do not fit: `bg-brand-red`, `text-brand-blue`, `border-brand-black`, etc.

## Backgrounds

Light backgrounds only from: `brand-white`, `brand-beige`, `brand-pink` (or semantic `background`, `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`).

## Accents

- Default accent color is **red** (`brand-red` / `destructive` / `chart-1`).
- Blue and pink are for **additional** series, badges, or decorative blocks — not the primary CTA unless specified.
- Do not use blue as the default button or link color.

## Dark mode

Dark mode inverts black ↔ white via CSS variables. Accents (red, blue, pink, beige) stay the same. Use semantic tokens; do not hardcode `#000` / `#fff` in components.

## Borders, hover, disabled

Opacity on black/white is allowed via semantic tokens:

- `border-border`, `ring-ring`, `text-muted-foreground`
- `bg-primary/80`, `hover:bg-muted`, `opacity-50` for disabled states

Do not invent new gray scales.

## Forbidden

- Raw hex in TSX/CSS (`#0212EE`, `rgb(...)`)
- Tailwind default color scales (`gray-*`, `blue-*`, `red-*` except `brand-*`)
- New colors outside the six brand tokens without design approval

